+
+// Redoubt LW-M7-45: "Delete browsing data on quit" also covers sessions that
+// did not end through the Quit menu item.
+//
+// Upstream deletes the selected categories only when the user picks Quit
+// (MenuDialogFragment -> DeleteBrowsingDataController.clearBrowsingDataOnQuit).
+// Swiping the app away from recents, an OOM kill, a crash, a force-stop or a
+// reboot skips the deletion, and the next start restores the tabs, cookies and
+// history the user asked to have deleted. Owner decisions 2026-10-06: "lets
+// build both as fallback"; trigger rule "Every non-Quit exit"; link starts
+// "Yes, hard gate".
+//
+//   (b) the guarantee, bounded. A marker file records how the session ended:
+//       "clean" is written only after Quit's deletion has been confirmed;
+//       every other end leaves "running" (or "cleaning") behind. On a cold
+//       start with the setting on and a marker that is not "clean",
+//       FenixApplication runs the same deletion for the selected categories:
+//       the engine deletions (and the site-permissions DB, which needs the
+//       main thread) are dispatched asynchronously before any activity exists;
+//       the local stores (Places, session file, recently closed tabs,
+//       thumbnails, downloads DB) are deleted on the IO dispatcher while the
+//       main thread waits for them, bounded (5 s). The cold-start gate opens
+//       when Gecko and every store confirmed, or after ENGINE_TIMEOUT_MS
+//       (20 s) counted from the start of the deletion. Until it opens, the
+//       session and downloads restores wait, and DeleteOnQuitStartGateMiddleware
+//       holds every engine-session creation -- so no page loads, whether it
+//       comes from the restore, a link (VIEW intent), a custom tab, a PWA or a
+//       widget/shortcut. With HISTORY selected and TABS kept, the restored
+//       tabs lose their back/forward history (the equivalent of upstream's
+//       EngineAction.PurgeHistoryAction on Quit). A deletion that itself kills
+//       the process cannot loop: the attempt count is in the marker, written
+//       before the deletion starts, and after MAX_ATTEMPTS the start continues
+//       without deleting and logs an error.
+//
+//       The bound is deliberate: if the engine has not confirmed within 20 s,
+//       or a local step fails, the gate opens anyway (fail open, logged as
+//       "deletion incomplete") and browsing continues; the marker is
+//       "running" again, so the deletion is retried after the next exit that
+//       is not Quit.
+//
+//   (a) best effort. DeleteOnQuitTaskService (stopWithTask="false") is started
+//       at every activity start, so Android calls onTaskRemoved when the task
+//       is swiped away. That starts the same deletion without waiting for it;
+//       Android usually kills the process within milliseconds, so (a) may not
+//       finish -- (b) does not depend on it.
+//
+// Nothing here touches the network, and with the setting off nothing is
+// deleted or held. Log tag: RedoubtDeleteOnQuit.
+
